      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Kitchen temperature fluctuations directly influence the metabolic rates of both yeast and lactobacillus, often causing sudden pH drops when warmer conditions accelerate fermentation. While flour protein does affect dough strength and extensibility, it plays a less direct role in the immediate acid spikes compared to ambient heat. To stabilize your starter, focus primarily on maintaining a consistent, cool environment to balance microbial activity rather than adjusting your flour blend.",
      "source": "target",
