    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i guess i focused too much on the flour. so if i'm seeing these spikes, is it basically just the lactobacillus running away with the process when it gets too warm? it feels like the balance just gets completely hijacked. how do i actually measure the rate of change to know if i'm nearing a point where the acidity becomes unmanageable?",
