      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just so frustrating cause it feels like the moment i turn my back last night, the whole thing just goes wild. it's like the microbes have a mind of their own and just decide to act up at the worst possible time. is there any way to actually moderate that \"unruly\" behavior so it's more predictable? like, can i actually control the specific ratio of yeast to bacteria to prevent those sudden shifts?",
